# Written by `autonomous-sdlc-harness init`, and yours from there on: edit it freely, a
# re-run keeps your copy.
#
# Line-ending normalisation only. Everything else a repository puts in this file - diff
# drivers, merge strategies, linguist hints, filters - is a project decision the harness
# has no opinion about, so it starts empty and you add to it.

# Store every text file with LF whatever the contributing machine writes it with.
* text=auto

# ...and check the executable assets out with LF on every platform. A script is run by
# the interpreter named on its `#!` line, and a CR at the end of that line is read as
# part of the interpreter's name: a CRLF checkout fails with "bad interpreter" or
# "no such file or directory", neither of which mentions a line ending.
*.sh text eol=lf
githooks/* text eol=lf
